# MC-X-F12 (writer 9): L §4.3 rule 2, "a later version that gives it a dated row makes such a reader state `at`
# (LOAD-LAWDATE)". v2 replaces a row of rate from 2027-06, so rate is law-dated and r, which states no at, is
# refused.
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"

input age3: int
band rate(a: int): money PLN
def r[m in months]: money PLN = rate(age3)
ask q: r[2027-05]

version v_act
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  age3 = 3 "the age"
  rate: [0, 6) = 400.00 PLN "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"

version v2
  cite act
  governs 2027-06..
  known 2027-05-01
  replace rate: [0, 6) = 450.00 PLN "under 6, raised"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE r reads law-dated facts and states no at (m.tally:12)
